One command to fix everything. Run this exact block:

```bash
cd ~/Projects/Enconnex/custom/enconnex_account_report && \
cat > views/account_report_expanded_views.xml << 'EOF'
<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<odoo>
    <data>
        <record id="action_account_report_expanded_pdf" model="ir.actions.server">
            <field name="name">Expanded PDF</field>
            <field name="model_id" ref="account_reports.model_account_report"/>
            <field name="binding_model_id" ref="account_reports.model_account_report"/>
            <field name="state">code</field>
            <field name="code">action = model.action_print_expanded_pdf(env.context.get('report_options', {}))</field>
        </record>
        <record id="action_account_report_expanded_xlsx" model="ir.actions.server">
            <field name="name">Expanded XLSX</field>
            <field name="model_id" ref="account_reports.model_account_report"/>
            <field name="binding_model_id" ref="account_reports.model_account_report"/>
            <field name="state">code</field>
            <field name="code">action = model.action_print_expanded_xlsx(env.context.get('report_options', {}))</field>
        </record>
    </data>
</odoo>
EOF
echo "✅ XML file created" && \
ls -lh views/account_report_expanded_views.xml && \
ls -lh models/account_report_expanded.py && \
echo "✅ Both files exist. Now restart Odoo with -u enconnex_account_report"
```

## What this does

1. Goes to the module folder
2. Creates the XML file (overwrites if exists, no typo possible)
3. Verifies both required files exist
4. Tells you next step

## After running it

Stop Odoo in PyCharm (red ⏹), then click ▶ again (you should still have `-u enconnex_account_report` in Run Config from before).

## Reply

- ✅ "Odoo started, no errors" → test in browser
- ❌ New error → paste **last 15 lines only** (not the full traceback — just the error message lines)
